<body>

<header>
  <div class="container">
    <h1>UK Retail Fuel Price Trend Analysis</h1>
    <div class="subtitle">A comprehensive analysis of retail fuel pricing patterns across UK forecourts, examining price distributions by fuel type and temporal update behaviour based on government-mandated open data.</div>
    <div class="meta">Report Period: {date_min} – {date_max} &nbsp;|&nbsp; Generated: {datetime.now().strftime('%d %B %Y')} &nbsp;|&nbsp; Records Analysed: {total_records:,}</div>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="container">

<!-- KPI Cards -->
<div class="kpi-row">
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="value">{unique_stations:,}</div>
    <div class="label">Unique Stations</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="value">{total_records:,}</div>
    <div class="label">Total Price Records</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="value">{len(fuel_types)}</div>
    <div class="label">Fuel Types</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="value">{lag_stats['median']:.1f}h</div>
    <div class="label">Median Update Lag</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="value">{price_stats.loc['E10','Median'] if 'E10' in price_stats.index else 'N/A':.1f}p</div>
    <div class="label">Median E10 Price (ppl)</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Section 1: Dataset Overview -->
<section id="overview">
  <h2>1. Dataset Overview &amp; Coverage Summary</h2>
  <p>This report analyses <strong>{total_records:,}</strong> individual fuel price observations recorded across <strong>{unique_stations:,}</strong> unique UK forecourts. The data spans from <strong>{date_min}</strong> to <strong>{date_max}</strong>, covering approximately {(df['recorded_at'].max() - df['recorded_at'].min()).days} days of reporting activity.</p>

  <h3>Fuel Types Present</h3>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Fuel Type</th><th>Record Count</th><th>Share of Dataset</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {fuel_count_table()}
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Data Completeness</h3>
  {null_info()}

  <div class="insight-box">
    <strong>Coverage Note:</strong> The dataset includes {len(fuel_types)} distinct fuel types: {', '.join(fuel_types)}. Station identifiers are anonymised hashes, so geographic or brand-level analysis is not possible with this dataset alone.
  </div>
</section>

<!-- Section 2: Price Distribution by Fuel Type -->
<section id="price-by-fuel-type">
  <h2>2. Price Distribution by Fuel Type</h2>
  <p>The table below summarises key descriptive statistics for each fuel type. Prices are reported in pence per litre (ppl).</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Fuel Type</th><th>Count</th><th>Mean</th><th>Median</th><th>Std Dev</th><th>Min</th><th>Q1</th><th>Q3</th><th>Max</th><th>IQR</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {stats_table_rows()}
    </tbody>
  </table>

